Prompt words for Python script to generate scatter diagram
Write a Python script to generate a variety of scatter charts (1000 charts in total). Each chart should have a size of approximately 500×500 pixels, with both length and width allowed to fluctuate slightly around 500.
Each chart should include:
A coordinate axis with either a linear or logarithmic scale, randomly chosen, and a randomly positioned origin.
A legend box placed at a random location, optionally surrounded by a solid border (randomly determined). If a solid border is present, its size should adapt to the combined area of the legend symbols and their corresponding labels.
Legend entries (typically 2 per chart, though other quantities may occur with low probability) with randomized symbol shapes, colors, sizes, transparency ("virtual reality" likely refers to alpha/opacity), and line thickness. Each legend symbol and its descriptive English text should ideally appear on the same line.
Scatter points (approximately 10–50 per chart) should be randomly placed across the chart, potentially distributed in any quadrant of the axes. The style of the points must match one of the legend entries.
Finally, store the following typical features in JOSN format: X-axis label, Y-axis label, image name, legend box, legend shape area, legend text area, axis tick marks and scale lines, and pixel coordinates of scatter points for each symbol type. 
